    "President Prabowo Subianto proposed Sugiono and Andi Amran Sulaiman as vice presidential candidates to the MPR.",
    "The nominations aim to fill the vacant vice presidency following the departure of Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
    "The MPR verification team has initiated the formal process to review the two candidates for the remaining 2024-2029 term."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto has officially forwarded two names, Sugiono and Andi Amran Sulaiman, to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) to serve as vice presidential candidates. This move follows the departure of Gibran Rakabuming Raka from the vice presidency. Sugiono currently serves as the Coordinating Minister for Human Development and Cultural Affairs, while Andi Amran Sulaiman serves as the Minister of Agriculture. According to reports, the decision follows consultations with coalition parties and the Gerindra Party's Board of Trustees. The MPR, led by Ahmad Muzani, has established a verification team to begin the formal selection process for the 2024-2029 term. The succession involves several procedural stages before a new vice president is inaugurated, with candidates being evaluated based on their professional backgrounds, public service records, and stated financial disclosures submitted to the Corruption Eradication Commission.",
